    "intro_html":  "Kefta mkaouara is the Moroccan dish that taught the rest of the world you can build a whole dinner out of small spiced meatballs and a pot of tomatoes. Turkey kefta go in with paprika, cumin, cinnamon, and a fistful of cilantro, the sauce cooks down thick, and an egg finishes each portion. It runs \u003cstrong\u003e561 calories and 35 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$2.04\u003c/strong\u003e, which is a lot of flavor for pocket change.",
